# VSD synthesis vault — line-ending policy (load-bearing for the immutable harness).
#
# Notes under vsd-vault/notes/ are Ed25519-signed against their EXACT bytes — the harness
# (vsd-vault/.vsd/vsd_provenance.py::note_canonical_hash) hashes raw note bytes with NO
# line-ending normalization. The vault's committed signing form is CRLF, and the Synthesis
# Integrity Chain commits to the CRLF-signed PBSA manifests. Force CRLF on checkout so every
# signature verifies on every platform regardless of core.autocrlf — otherwise autocrlf smudges
# the LF-normalized blobs to CRLF (and a Linux checkout leaves them LF), the bytes change, and the
# harness fails closed on a hash mismatch (this is what stranded cycle 49 before 2026-06-28).
# See vsd-vault/orchestrator/SYNTHESIS_LOOP.md.
vsd-vault/notes/**/*.md text eol=crlf

# Sealed match artifacts — same policy, same reason.
#
# PoSP records, the tri-plane manifest, and the WMP corpus were sealed on Windows: the digests in
# the anchor files, the M17 match certificate, and provenance_dag_index_2026-07-12.json are all
# sha256 over the CRLF bytes. Checked out LF (any non-Windows clone, and CI), sha256 differs and
# every byte-identity check over them fails closed — the PORT-CERT anchor-digest check (C4) and
# verify_provenance_dag both report a mismatch that is purely line endings. Force CRLF so the
# sealed bytes are reproduced on every platform.
audits/posp_record_*.json text eol=crlf
audits/tri_plane_manifest_*.json text eol=crlf
wmp_corpus_real/wmp_corpus.jsonl text eol=crlf
